WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.076 --> 00:00:07.188
- Next up is Mihovail talking
about New Years' Resolutions.

00:00:07.188 --> 00:00:08.881
So, that's timely here.

00:00:08.881 --> 00:00:11.189
He's said he's trying to
change his approach this year

00:00:11.189 --> 00:00:14.406
to focus on not making
a list of resolutions,

00:00:14.406 --> 00:00:17.819
but making a list of
mistakes and explanations

00:00:17.819 --> 00:00:21.205
to look at why he didn't follow through

00:00:21.205 --> 00:00:22.315
on making those plans

00:00:22.315 --> 00:00:24.518
and fixing the mistakes from last year.

00:00:24.518 --> 00:00:27.828
What are our thoughts
and how do you go about

00:00:27.828 --> 00:00:31.572
making resolutions, or even
do you for the new year?

00:00:31.572 --> 00:00:34.270
- For the New Year, I'm
going to try one thing, Evan,

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:36.204
because I'm so conscious.

00:00:36.204 --> 00:00:39.670
I bust my own chops, I'll be honest.

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:42.337
I demand a lot from myself.

00:00:42.337 --> 00:00:45.678
I never think when I look at
myself I've done well enough,

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:48.272
and that's kind of deep
lingering in my psyche.

00:00:48.272 --> 00:00:52.284
I think, and this is advice
I'd give to everybody,

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:53.971
when you look at yourselves,

00:00:53.971 --> 00:00:57.258
we've got great people today
joined us for the blab,

00:00:57.258 --> 00:01:00.739
I think I'm going to try
in the New Year to say,

00:01:00.739 --> 00:01:02.790
not for me but for other people,

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.529
just look for the good things they did,

00:01:04.529 --> 00:01:06.233
and it's almost back to sports.

00:01:06.233 --> 00:01:09.530
If you're competing against
kind of, I don't know,

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:12.194
say, Usain Bolt, for the 100 Meters,

00:01:12.194 --> 00:01:14.255
do you beat yourself up all the time

00:01:14.255 --> 00:01:15.915
on that 1/100th of a second

00:01:15.915 --> 00:01:17.362
where you don't come out the blocks?

00:01:17.362 --> 00:01:19.672
Or do you celebrate the
things that you do well

00:01:19.672 --> 00:01:21.614
in the last 50 meters where you accelerate

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.603
away from everybody else?

00:01:23.603 --> 00:01:27.589
I think we should, as
leaders, focus way more

00:01:27.589 --> 00:01:30.852
on the things we do well,
and make them even better,

00:01:30.852 --> 00:01:35.019
and if we do that, I think we'll
find we make less mistakes,

00:01:36.289 --> 00:01:39.708
and also, any sort of
improvements we need,

00:01:39.708 --> 00:01:41.336
you can call them
whatever you want really.

00:01:41.336 --> 00:01:43.129
We've all got weaknesses.

00:01:43.129 --> 00:01:46.521
But, if you accentuate the positives,

00:01:46.521 --> 00:01:49.623
and if you've got people working
for you in your businesses,

00:01:49.623 --> 00:01:51.729
if you just give them
a bit of praise about

00:01:51.729 --> 00:01:54.544
what efforts they've put
in to achieving something

00:01:54.544 --> 00:01:58.722
that was connected to your big
passion, and dream, and idea,

00:01:58.722 --> 00:01:59.605
then, wow.

00:01:59.605 --> 00:02:02.881
You'll make them rise 40,000ft,

00:02:02.881 --> 00:02:05.445
and fly out of your home office,

00:02:05.445 --> 00:02:07.883
and they'll be able to rule the world.

00:02:07.883 --> 00:02:09.903
And I think so often when I look,

00:02:09.903 --> 00:02:13.784
and I say this for myself in
terms of one learning for me,

00:02:13.784 --> 00:02:16.744
it's so easy to say,
"Oh you did this. Okay,

00:02:16.744 --> 00:02:18.705
"but I want to tell you
about these three things

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:20.573
"that you didn't do so good."

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:23.024
And the voice in your head,

00:02:23.024 --> 00:02:24.952
because a lot of overcoming the fear

00:02:24.952 --> 00:02:27.725
is smashing down the walls,

00:02:27.725 --> 00:02:31.139
and smashing those voices that
tell you you can't do stuff

00:02:31.139 --> 00:02:32.916
because you know you can.

00:02:32.916 --> 00:02:35.283
You know you can, and
if you keep on listening

00:02:35.283 --> 00:02:37.747
to the voices around you or in your head,

00:02:37.747 --> 00:02:39.257
they'll just grind you down,

00:02:39.257 --> 00:02:40.659
and you kind of just
lose the will to live.

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:43.538
So, I do think, actually,
both for yourself,

00:02:43.538 --> 00:02:46.092
it's really good to
celebrate the positive,

00:02:46.092 --> 00:02:48.138
to savor the moment, but most of all,

00:02:48.138 --> 00:02:51.707
if you're a company of
two, three, five people,

00:02:51.707 --> 00:02:54.386
wouldn't it be powerful
when you've won a big order

00:02:54.386 --> 00:02:56.524
to take everybody out for dinner,

00:02:56.524 --> 00:02:58.136
and just celebrate that and enjoy it,

00:02:58.136 --> 00:02:59.776
and say "Your contribution was this,

00:02:59.776 --> 00:03:01.792
"and if we hadn't won that."

00:03:01.792 --> 00:03:04.276
It maybe be a pitch or it maybe
the product they invented,

00:03:04.276 --> 00:03:05.766
or whatever.

00:03:05.766 --> 00:03:09.450
It's so powerful to
galvanize the people together

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:12.832
against your passion for your dream.

00:03:12.832 --> 00:03:16.693
So, one thing I do is in terms
of the New Years Resolution,

00:03:16.693 --> 00:03:20.114
yeah, okay, spend maybe 20%
of your time when you do that

00:03:20.114 --> 00:03:23.630
on the one mistake, but
actually spend 80% of the time

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:26.564
on the things you did really, really well,

00:03:26.564 --> 00:03:29.261
and then you become a
super trained athlete

00:03:29.261 --> 00:03:31.764
to do them over better, and, you know,

00:03:31.764 --> 00:03:33.039
focus on the positive.

00:03:33.039 --> 00:03:36.218
- To Steven's point, I would encourage you

00:03:36.218 --> 00:03:38.485
to not just wait 'til
the New Years' Resolution

00:03:38.485 --> 00:03:39.837
to come around to start doing it.

00:03:39.837 --> 00:03:43.490
If Steven inspired you with
that story about celebrating

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:46.684
the win, then today is the resolution.

00:03:46.684 --> 00:03:48.096
Like, do it right now.

00:03:48.096 --> 00:03:50.404
So many people wait until the
New Year to start something,

00:03:50.404 --> 00:03:53.841
and then they fall off
track a couple weeks in.

00:03:53.841 --> 00:03:56.863
I would love for you guys
listening and watching,

00:03:56.863 --> 00:03:58.400
for entrepreneurs, to when you get an idea

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.709
just go out and try it.

00:04:00.709 --> 00:04:03.605
Even if you don't know
all the details, right?

00:04:03.605 --> 00:04:05.725
So, I want to celebrate a win.

00:04:05.725 --> 00:04:06.561
Okay, great.

00:04:06.561 --> 00:04:07.595
Is it going to be a restaurant?

00:04:07.595 --> 00:04:08.956
Is it going to be with a gift certificate?

00:04:08.956 --> 00:04:11.701
You start planning all the things out,

00:04:11.701 --> 00:04:13.624
the perfectionists in us,
planning all the things out.

00:04:13.624 --> 00:04:15.442
You make it some big thing,

00:04:15.442 --> 00:04:17.072
and then because it's
so big we never do it.

00:04:17.072 --> 00:04:18.564
Because it has to be the perfect thing,

00:04:18.564 --> 00:04:20.435
and we never do anything.

00:04:20.435 --> 00:04:22.008
And I think just starting something small,

00:04:22.008 --> 00:04:24.511
it could be a phone call, it
could be taking somebody out,

00:04:24.511 --> 00:04:27.831
it could be just buying
them a Starbucks, whatever,

00:04:27.831 --> 00:04:29.526
just try something.

00:04:29.526 --> 00:04:31.463
See how it feels, and adjust.

00:04:31.463 --> 00:04:33.219
And I would love for you
guys to get in the habit

00:04:33.219 --> 00:04:36.074
of constantly doing the self evaluation

00:04:36.074 --> 00:04:38.839
and checking yourself,
and not waiting until

00:04:38.839 --> 00:04:43.805
New Years' or your birthday,
or some other arbitrary day.

00:04:43.805 --> 00:04:45.072
Like, just start doing it.

00:04:45.072 --> 00:04:47.138
You get inspired by something
you hear today, take action!

00:04:47.138 --> 00:04:50.193
That would make both Steven
and myself insanely happy.

00:04:50.193 --> 00:04:51.805
That's the goal, right?

00:04:51.805 --> 00:04:53.765
Don't wait another,
you know, couple weeks.

00:04:53.765 --> 00:04:55.617
Do something today.

00:04:55.617 --> 00:04:58.114
- Yeah, I think, Evan, as well,
that's such a great point.

00:04:58.114 --> 00:04:59.992
And, you know, another great quote,

00:04:59.992 --> 00:05:03.336
"Never leave til tomorrow
what can be done today."

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:06.201
And, I think, you know,
why wait til the New Year?

00:05:06.201 --> 00:05:08.716
This is a great holiday season,

00:05:08.716 --> 00:05:11.279
and for you guys who've
got customers out there,

00:05:11.279 --> 00:05:14.422
and if you got people working for you,

00:05:14.422 --> 00:05:17.354
colleagues that work for
you and follow your dream,

00:05:17.354 --> 00:05:20.800
what a golden time to say a
really heartfelt thank you

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.394
in the holiday season.

00:05:22.394 --> 00:05:24.289
It's sort of a time to pause, reflect.

00:05:24.289 --> 00:05:27.103
They're going to go home with
their families, or friends,

00:05:27.103 --> 00:05:29.590
and it's a really a pretty cool time

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:31.580
to pick up the phone to customers,

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:34.279
send them a SMS or a direct message,

00:05:34.279 --> 00:05:36.694
just saying "Thank you so much

00:05:36.694 --> 00:05:38.550
"for your custom over this year.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:41.772
"I'm really excited about
working with you again in 2017."

00:05:41.772 --> 00:05:45.772
So, this is a great time,
not just the new year,

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:49.467
but the end of the year, just to celebrate

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:51.032
what you've achieved this year,

00:05:51.032 --> 00:05:54.731
recognize a few other people,
especially your customers,

00:05:54.731 --> 00:05:56.321
and the people who've built that,

00:05:56.321 --> 00:05:57.918
which is the people you employ.

00:05:57.918 --> 00:06:01.027
Just say thank you very much.

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:02.166
It's a good time,

00:06:02.166 --> 00:06:04.611
and I think everybody
wants to feel valued,

00:06:04.611 --> 00:06:06.303
and the more you do that, again,

00:06:06.303 --> 00:06:10.807
it's kind of weird, there's
this flywheel of positivity

00:06:10.807 --> 00:06:12.602
because if you say that to your colleagues

00:06:12.602 --> 00:06:14.322
and you say that to your customer

00:06:14.322 --> 00:06:16.878
they're feeling the love your big idea,

00:06:16.878 --> 00:06:19.878
and they'll give you great feedback.

